    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to present No. 24 Woodberry to the market, a beautifully presented five-bedroom detached family home with a converted attic room finished to an exceptionally high standard, extending to approx.180 sq.mtrs (c.1,938 sq.ft) and ideally situated on a site that is not directly overlooked front or rear, the property also benefits from having a South facing rear garden. This exclusive enclave of detached homes offers a peaceful setting while remaining convenient to a wide range of amenities given its location just off the Carpenterstown Road. \n\nThe property comes to the market in excellent condition and has had many upgrades and quality finishes added over the years by the current owners. On entering, a welcoming and spacious hallway immediately sets the tone, with well-proportioned reception rooms located on either side — a formal living room to the left and a comfortable family room to the right, ideal for everyday living and entertaining. To the rear of the home is a formal dining room that opens into the bright and open-plan kitchen/breakfast area and enjoying views over the rear garden. A separate utility room off the kitchen and a guest WC off the hallway add to the home's practicality for family life.\n\nUpstairs, the accommodation continues to impress with five generously sized bedrooms, two of which benefit from en-suite fully tiled shower rooms, along with a large, bright and well-appointed family bathroom. The current owners also added an attic conversion which offers extra reception room as well as a home office. \n\nTo the front, the property is not directly overlooked and is only 1 of 3 properties along the cul-de-sac enhancing its sense of privacy and appeal. It also overlooks a large green area ideal for young families. A cobble-lock driveway provides off-street parking and leads to dual gated side access. The rear garden is fully landscaped with a lawned area bordered by mature flower beds, specimen trees and shrubs and a large paved limestone patio area, an ideal space for al fresco dining and home entertaining. A fully insulated steel metal shed provides valuable additional storage.\n\nWoodberry is located just off the Carpenterstown Road, where there is a wide range of local amenities just a stone's throw from your doorstep, to include a Spar, The Carpenter Bar & Restaurant, a pharmacy and café, as well as numerous parks and playgrounds. There is also a choice of schools within easy reach, such as Castleknock College, Mount Sackville Girls School, Castleknock Community College, St. Patricks National School and Scoil Thomas (School admission policies can change and must be verified). Coolmine Train Station is just an 8 minute walk approx., as well as having a good bus service available, making commuting to and from the city centre a breeze. Castleknock and Blanchardstown villages are just a 5 minute drive approx, with even more amenities to choose from, as well as the wonderful Blanchardstown Shopping Centre.\n\nThis is a wonderful opportunity to acquire a spacious and versatile family home in a highly sought-after location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 2.94m x 2.68m\nBright and welcoming hallway, with feature coving. Hardwood Oak Junckers flooring\n\nGuest WC - 1.57m x 0.8m\nComprising of a wash hand basin and wc, fully tiled.\n\nFamily Room - 3.3m x 2.6m\nLocated to the right of the hallway, additional reception room with coving and Hardwood Oak Junckers flooring, door to kitchen.\n\nLiving Room - 4.48m x 4.5m\nThis is a very generously proportioned and elegant room with feature bay window. There is a feature Oak surround fireplace (solid fuel) with cast iron inset. Bespoke fitted storage shelving and presses to either side. Hardwood Oak Junckers flooring. Coving and centre rose. Double Oak doors to dining room.\n\nDining Room - 4.5m x 3m\nOverlooking the rear garden this formal dining room is ideal for entertaining, sliding doors lead to the rear patio. Hardwood Oak Junckers flooring. Door to kitchen.\n\nKitchen/Breakfast room - 5.15m x 3.62m\nFully Fitted in 2019 this modern kitchen contains a hand made in-frame kitchen with an excellent selection of floor and eye level presses and a Belfast style sink with quartz worktops. There is a good range of integrated high end appliances including gas hob, extractor fan, dishwasher, double oven and grill. This open plan space enjoys views of the rear garden and there are double doors leading to the rear garden/patio. Tiled flooring. There is also access to some extra under stair storage.\n\nUtility Room - 2.91m x 1.4m\nPlumbed for a washing machine and a dryer there is a sink and fitted cabinets and storage as well as a gas boiler. Side door opens to the rear garden. Tiled flooring and partly tiled walls.\n\nLanding - 4.72m x1.8m\nWith Hot-press and stairs to attic room.\n\nPrimary Bedroom - 4.56mx 3.6m\nA beautiful main bedroom with feature Bay window, fully fitted wardrobes and solid Walnut timber flooring.\n\nEn-Suite - 1.6m x 1.53m\nFitted in 2025 this modern and stylish en-suite is fully tiled and contains a corner shower, wc and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.7m x 3m\nLarge double bedroom with fitted wardrobes and semi solid Oak timber flooring.\n\nEn-Suite - 2.3m x 0.75m\nBright fully tiled en-suite with shower, wc and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.48m x 2.86m\nLocated to the rear of the house double bedroom with hardwood Oak timber flooring\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.71m x 2.45m\nLocated to the rear of the house double bedroom with hardwood Oak timber flooring\n\nBedroom 5 - 3m x 2.33m\nGood sized single bedroom with built in wardrobes.\n\nBathroom - 2m x 1.48m\nLarge bright family bathroom fully tiled, with bath wc and wash hand basin.\n\nAttic Room/ Office - 5.96m x 3.45m\nA great addition to the property is this large attic room that has been finished to an excepionatly high standard and offers extra reception space, ideal for a variety of uses, there is a built-in study/office area with shelving as well as good access to eaves storage. 2 Velux roof lights offer plenty of natural light, solid Chestnut timber flooring.\n\nSteel Shed - \nInsulated steel metal shed, Ideal workshop and for extra home storage, power supply.\n\n"
      },
